## 1. How the buds work together day to day

Who does what (role text read from the charters):
- VERIFIED Dobby: second brain of Yim and fleet coordinator; takes work from Yim, does it itself when it can, coordinates the team, follows through. `fleet/dobby.yaml` L21-25. Root soul; jizo and osaa sprouted from it (L22-23). Decision tiers: small = Dobby decides and reports, moderate = collaborate, big = Yim decides (`fleet/dobby.yaml` task_tiers).
- VERIFIED Daruma: product manager and pace-setter; sets goals and chases them to done. `fleet/daruma.yaml` L20.
- VERIFIED Kensa: adversarial reviewer and security steward. `fleet/kensa.yaml` L38.
- VERIFIED Jizo: the fleet's senses; reads channels, verifies what is real. `fleet/jizo.yaml` L19; also public page.
- VERIFIED Mamori: infrastructure and delivery. `fleet/mamori.yaml` L29. Incidents are mamori's standing duty, not Dobby's, with kensa refuting the postmortem (`fleet/INVARIANTS.md` section 13).
- VERIFIED Fude (writing), Osaa (images), Koe (marketing), Aida (UX/service design), Kura (treasury), Hako (operations), Ryo (quant), Sora (IoT), Kokoro (philosophy companion), Yojo (body care): roles per `fleet/FLEET-BIBLE.md` member table and the public page (Yojo only in the Bible).

Handoff between buds:
- VERIFIED Work moves as files, not chat. A signed envelope (HMAC) goes into an inbox folder the receiving daemon polls: `fleet/README.md` L270-291; `fleet/INVARIANTS.md` section 11 (Yim's quote: Discord is the outer layer, files are the protocol). Unsigned envelopes are rejected in strict mode (README L289).
- VERIFIED Why: a chat-triggered bot runs read-only, so a handoff that needs to write a file died silently; real case in README L277-283.
- VERIFIED Discord rooms are where a human talks to a bud (one bud, one seat). README L266-269.
- VERIFIED Busy bud queues work and replies with a machine-readable acknowledgment; replies matched by id, not time. `ψ/writing/book-fleet/md/ch07.md` 7.1-7.2.
- VERIFIED Permission to edit files belongs to the person who ordered the work, not to a bud that forwarded it; forwarded work is read-only. `ch07.md` 7.3.
- VERIFIED Larger tasks carry a goal card (what done means, checks, how much autonomy, when to stop and ask); Daruma counts "done" from the card's checks, not from a bud saying "done". `fleet/INVARIANTS.md` section 8.

Who checks whose work:
- VERIFIED No self-review: the maker may not be its own checker. `fleet/INVARIANTS.md` section 9.
- VERIFIED Checker must run on a different model, and for anything that leaves the house a different vendor (text: koe plus Codex; images: osaa plus Codex; irreversible: prism-swarm). INVARIANTS section 9 ("Widened 2026-10-02"); `fleet/REVIEW-MATRIX.md` outward-content row.
- VERIFIED Two review axes: technical (Kensa) and product (Daruma). REVIEW-MATRIX "สองแกนของ review".
- VERIFIED Review routing is risk-based: docs-only needs none; auth/secrets/deploy needs a security review. REVIEW-MATRIX matrix.

Where humans approve:
- VERIFIED Irreversible actions (delete, push, merge to main, spend money, send email, post, deploy to production) need Yim's approval by DM; approval in a room does not count. `fleet/dobby.yaml` persona (FLEET_DM_OWNER line); INVARIANTS section 5 ("Merge to main without human approval" is forbidden).
- VERIFIED Handbook table "ทำเองแล้วรายงาน / ต้องให้คนตัดสิน": publishing publicly, things whose result belongs to someone else, irreversible things need a person. `ch08.md` 8.4.
- VERIFIED Yim is reachable after work hours only for critical issues; items waiting on her go up before 19:00. INVARIANTS section 10.
- VERIFIED Memory is files plus a graph index; files are canonical. `fleet/FLEET-ARCHITECTURE.md` "Brain delivery".
